Virtual Inheritance in C++

 *Description* 

This C++ program demonstrates multiple inheritance and virtual inheritance using "Person", "Student", "Employee", and "TeachingAssistant" classes.

The "TeachingAssistant" class inherits from both "Student" and "Employee", while both classes virtually inherit from "Person". This ensures that only one copy of the "Person" class is created.

 *Concepts Used* 

- Classes and Objects
- Inheritance
- Multiple Inheritance
- Virtual Inheritance
- Constructor
- Protected Data Members
- "std::string"

 *Class Structure* 

          Person
         /      \
   Student    Employee
         \      /
     TeachingAssistant

 *Working* 

- "Person" stores the person's name.
- "Student" and "Employee" virtually inherit from "Person".
- "TeachingAssistant" inherits from both "Student" and "Employee".
- "TeachingAssistant" directly initializes the "Person" constructor with the name ""Riya"".
- "displayName()" displays the name.

 *Sample Output* 

Name: Riya

 *Objective* 

To understand virtual inheritance and how it solves the diamond problem in C++ multiple inheritance.
